      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4d34d07d-1996-5807-a857-c2f65fff1a38",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Peter Capaldi, Ben Whishaw, Paul King, Simon Farnaby, David Heyman, Jenna Coleman, Samuel Anderson\n- Products: Doctor Who, The Thick of It, Paddington, Paddington 2, Into the Dalek, Skyfall, Spectre\n- Roles: the Doctor, Malcolm Tucker, Mr. Curry, Danny Pink, Q, Paddington Bear\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Capaldi was born on 14 April 1958 and is a Scottish actor, writer, and director.\n- Peter Capaldi is best known for playing the twelfth Doctor in Doctor Who and Malcolm Tucker in The Thick of It.\n- Peter Capaldi received four British Academy Television Award nominations for The Thick of It and won Best Male Comedy Performance in 2010.\n- Ben Whishaw played Q in the James Bond films Skyfall in 2012 and Spectre in 2015.\n- Peter Capaldi played Mr. Curry, Paddington Bear's neighbour, in the film Paddington.\n- Into the Dalek stars Peter Capaldi and Jenna Coleman and introduces Samuel Anderson as Danny Pink.\n- Paddington 2 is an upcoming British-French family-comedy film directed by Paul King, co-written by Paul King and Simon Farnaby, and produced by David Heyman.\n- Peter Capaldi was set to reprise Mr. Curry in Paddington 2.\n- Paddington 2 was set to be released on 10 November 2017.\n- Ben Whishaw voiced Paddington Bear in Paddington in 2014 and in Paddington 2 in 2017.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "f2981b09-32e6-5c3f-9c0d-c3e1d9833e71",
        "text": "Page: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: Peter Dougan Capaldi (born 14 April 1958) is a Scottish actor, writer and director, best known for playing the twelfth incarnation of the Doctor in \"Doctor Who\" and as spin doctor Malcolm Tucker in \"The Thick of It\", for which he has received four British Academy Television Award nominations, winning Best Male Comedy Performance in 2010.\nPage: Peter Capaldi. Sentence: He further took on the role of Paddington Bear's neighbour Mr. Curry in the family comedy film \"Paddington\"; he is set to reprise the role in \"Paddington 2\".\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: Paddington 2 is an upcoming British-French family-comedy film directed by Paul King, co written by King and Simon Farnaby, and produced by David Heyman.\nPage: Paddington 2. Sentence: The film is set to release on 10 November 2017.\nPage: Into the Dalek. Sentence: Starring Peter Capaldi and Jenna Coleman the episode also introduces Samuel Anderson as Danny Pink.\nPage: Ben Whishaw. Sentence: He has also played the role of Q in the James Bond films \"Skyfall\" (2012) and \"Spectre\" (2015), as well being the voice of Paddington Bear in \"Paddington\" (2014) and \"Paddington 2\" (2017).",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
